  Dragon scales seem like obvious armor for any non-winged non-giant
monster.  I doubt they come off of the dead dragon pre-fitted for
humans.  Allow the player to 'a'pply the dragon scales to essentially
drape them on the horse.  Probably not allow armoring a horse that's
saddled.  

 Any time the horse has a move when it's draped with dragon scales, but
isn't saddled, there's a 0.50 chance of the scales sliding off.

  To convert dragon scales into dragon scale mail tailored for a
pony/horse/warhorse the player has to polymorph into the target form,
wear the dragon scales, then read a non-cursed(?) scroll of enchant
armor.  The newly formed equine armor will be fitted to whichever of the
size of the equine monster the player has polyed into.   The new DSM can
be further enchanted according to the usual rules, subject to the player
shape requirements above.

  Might limit monster-specific armor like this to equine pets.  (Not
sure there would be a demand for dog/cat tailored armor.)  Is there a
large demand for armor for other monster shapes?



  Ponies are medium size monsters, horses and warhorses are large.

  So that only a pony can wear DSM tailored by a player polyed into pony
form when the DSM was created.  If the pony gains XL and becomes 
a horse while wearing the pony-DSM, the new horse breaks out of the
pony-DSM, destroying the armor.   This shouldn't be a real problem for
the player, just add some flavor to the whole concept.

  Equine tailored DSM will never fall off of a (war)horse, whether the
steed is saddled or not.   The #loot command might need to be enhanced
to allow the ability to remove the scales/armor from a steed.  Cursed
armor of course cannot be removed from the pet.  /oCanc seems the only
approach here (or death of the pet.)  /oCanc would also remove any extra
enchantment on the equine-armor.  (Not sure if armor removal is really
necessary.)

  As a semi-easter-egg, equine-tailored DSM armor at +0 will revert to
dragon scales if a c?oEA is read while the tailored armor is worn.  (I
think I pity any player who finds that useful.)


  So the player will require polycontrol, the ability to poly, extra
dragon scales, at least one extra non-cursed ?oEA, a saddle, and a tame
equine pet.  The ability to give a tame equine monster 10-14 more points
of AC, plus a dragon resistance, should have interesting results.




  


